  "note_id": "FN-OP_IMPLICIT_INTERSECTION-001",
  "functions": [
    "FUNC.OP_IMPLICIT_INTERSECTION"
  ],
  "kind": "quirk",
  "title": "Implicit intersection (@ / _xlfn.SINGLE) intersects ranges by caller position, takes array[1,1], and gives #REF! on 3-D",
  "statement": "In Excel 16.0.20527, @x reduces a single-area reference to the cell matching the formula's row (for multi-row) and column (for multi-column), returning #VALUE! when the caller lies outside the area or over a multi-area union (in row 20, @Data!A1:A3 evaluates to #VALUE!, ISREF(@Data!A1:A3) is FALSE, and TYPE(@Data!A1:A3) is 16, whereas in row 2, =QUOTIENT(12,+@Data!A1:A3) returns 2). On an array, @ takes element (1,1) without propagating off-corner errors (N(@{5,6}) = 5, ERROR.TYPE(@{1,#N/A}) = #N/A). On a 3-D reference, =@Ja:Ma!A1 returns #REF!. In .xlsx files, nested @x saves as _xlfn.SINGLE(x) while top-level @x in an ordinary formula drops @; both SINGLE(A1) and _xlfn.SINGLE(A1) are accepted at worksheet entry.",
  "status": "measured",
  "basis": "Measured across Excel 16.0.20527 in fn2_questions (fn2_q132, fn2_q141-q146), dc_nzpw (rows 8, 88, 111, 128, 147), l3 (F rows 1-2), eng13_legacy (q02, q04), hjd (row 9), and excel-entry.tsv (SINGLE and _xlfn.SINGLE rows).",
  "inferred": null,
  "documentation": null,
